Z||000000||digital wizard||02-26-2000||03:51 PM||||I have an 84 fiero SE 4 cyl. It drive's very nice and i love the car. i have it just for fun. it misses one thing POWER !!!!!<P>I want to build a Quad 4 HO engine into the fiero with a turbo. i think that will do the job to get more power. Is there anyone out there who has tried the same? and did you succeed ?<P>I know the al the facts and in the past i build an turbo on a 81' mustang that performed very good (until my waist gate got stuck and had a pressure of 1,5 bar, it was the fastest 0 to 100 km ever but also the last.  <P>i am searching for company's that supply an kit to swap the engine or whatever suggestion.......... ( it has to be a four cylinder because in the netherlands they wont' accept a V8, i tried that ) ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Phil||02-26-2000||04:12 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.americancustomeng.com" TARGET=_blank>www.americancustomeng.com</A>   makes such a kit||||reg||1
Z||000002||pherder||02-26-2000||04:25 PM||||digital wizard,<P>I wouldn't advise putting anything that adds pressure to a Quad 4.<P>They have problems just holding the head gasket under normal running ... turbo or supercharging would make the problem worst!<P>The ACE turbo HO Quad 4 I have seen blew it's head gasket in ONE run!  It did go fast ... for a little while.  That engine never ran right after that.<P>Paul<BR>88 Coupe w/HO Quad 4<BR>88 Formula to get a TPI V8<BR>88 GT getting a 3.1<BR>||||reg||13
Z||000003||terryk||02-26-2000||04:57 PM||||Do some poking around. There are a fiew Quad's with Eaton M-62's on them. Might be easier to install. Just build a new intake to sit the blower on.<P>The HO's are 10:1-ish, I admit that's very high for boost. Bet you can't run more than 6-8 of advance.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||02-28-2000||03:42 AM||||I owned one of ACE's turbo quad  4 "abortions".  I bought it from a guy who literally spent over $25000 on the car.  It was an '85 GT and had the Ryane slalom 1 coilover setup with an '88 cradle/rear suspension along with the Wilwood 12" brakes.  It out handled and out stopped almost every car out there, but the engine was the weak link.  Not more than 2 weeks after buying it the turbo died.  I replaced the turbo and within a month I had burnt a piston....leaned it out.  The quality (if you can call it that) of the ACE conversion was severely lacking.  I would highly recommend AGAINST using their products and definitely against them touching your car.  <P>I sold that car to a mechanic at the Fiero Factory in Alabama (Jeremy), so if you see it think of me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>He has since installed a stock V-6 and it runs & drives like it should....man I miss that car! ||||reg||8
